  "text.5516fbae1bdb2becb2f0": "formulas",
  "text.914a40fca32accc0e06c": "formulas · 5 fields",
  "text.a9704281d08bcfd36d32": "EBIT - cash tax on EBIT + D&A - gross capital cash spending - increase in other operating working capital + increase in customer advances.",
  "text.4f49b1deb6437c6e9a23": "capital Cash Spending",
  "text.81556475e22e70ffbe16": "PPE/intangible cash purchases + capital supplier advances not already in those purchases + capitalized site purchases. Reclassification of existing prepayments/CIP is not a new cash use.",
  "text.16553f238b45a98fa4cc": "customer Advances",
  "text.700bf1570029aca3a72e": "Ending = opening + new cash advances - recognized prepaid revenue - refunds (+ FX/acquisition adjustments where applicable).",
  "text.d2ee1287b4ec32a14c93": "funding Need",
  "text.5a4a81b5e4f4fcbb14df": "Peak cash uses + debt service + cash reserve - opening usable cash - net cash proceeds actually received - available committed credit draws. FCFF alone omits financing costs and principal maturity timing.",
  "text.2976e09e7ebc9b1b7339": "Terminal net reinvestment = terminal NOPAT * stable growth / terminal ROIC; customer-advance movement must be included consistently.",
  "text.982b2bb808c35fa4582c": "cautions · 4 records",
  "text.dcf72f14d47974d00d28": "All future investment schedules are analytical sensitivities anchored to disclosed spending/capacity, not disclosed future budgets. Cumulative peaks are not precise financing forecasts.",
  "text.eb97a494bbd93c94f65a": "Economic FCFF retains SBC as compensation expense. Strict cash liquidity adds back noncash SBC and separately subtracts award withholding/buybacks; modeled 1% AAOI and 3% NBIS SBC addbacks below are illustrations, and dilution must be recognized once.",
  "text.27f604dd1650e365c64a": "NBIS 2026 guide is modeled as cash-equivalent capital spending. If guidance includes accrued equipment additions, adjust payment timing and vendor-capital payables before using the H2 bridge. $973.3m H1 additions not yet paid cannot simply be added to cash capex twice.",
  "text.939e334534a2994b7bfa": "Annual average capacity and gross deployment are distinct. Margin, replacement cost and commissioning schedules must change coherently when the physical build or economic useful life changes.",
