  "text.7f58966f7a9e1fe0d7bf": "approximate_capex_outlook",
  "text.d25401a556d3ade82985": "AMZN-2026Q2-call",
  "text.806bf5da6cd39d972b58": "revised_approximate_cash_capex",
  "text.fe7c50d08fd44c8091e0": "Higher memory costs; not simply more installed capacity",
  "text.810007bf552779dde0ca": "longer horizon and aspirations",
  "text.ec605542bc0141111a27": "longer horizon and aspirations · 3 records",
  "text.bc45b5a5479148b72b27": "matched actual",
  "text.2211721630ec8db2b848": "AMZN-2025-letter",
  "text.24df6865d9cc3003fc2d": "AWS total power capacity",
  "text.cc589b22db4e2df37aac": "Double by end of 2027",
  "text.3a01459f99c1efc99b7e": "quantified_multi_year_operational_target",
  "text.805718f4c13fb6b2159c": "AWS annual revenue potential",
  "text.532d0179d22257beb042": "Possibly $1 trillion in time",
  "text.ce51b07c5419c134d645": "undated_aspiration_not_guidance",
  "text.3c8f50ea1c263768d6fb": "Trainium4 broad availability",
  "text.9701f5b919c30d1b39eb": "About 18 months from letter",
  "text.1b475fab0816775b8e49": "approximate_product_timeline",
  "text.82b47c7c4b4bacf73681": "coverage gaps",
  "text.62a2f2434f356b959694": "coverage gaps · 3 records",
  "text.3c987b358634bf19222b": "No complete historical annual capex revision series assembled for 2023–2025; quarterly revenue/EBIT sample is complete.",
  "text.581d30567b2816c29ef1": "No numerical AWS quarterly or multi-year revenue guidance in the reviewed releases; interviews are qualitative outlook or undated aspirations.",
  "text.bc8677e6cf7cc6d5935b": "Quarterly guide revisions outside routine releases not independently exhaustively searched; none found in reviewed source set.",
  "text.e904c9ccfa425ff0b055": "format",
  "text.a9f79a62529993cb8859": "Evidence-backed qualitative chart data, with no overall reputation score.",
  "text.a84435421ba9e93a1c5c": "Consistently conservative quarterly ranges with strong delivery. Long-horizon precision is not established.",
  "text.e0ee730262851990aca5": "High for measured quarterly outcomes; medium for interpretation.",
  "text.7f98b4c0f89ba65b788e": "Revenue exceeded the original upper range in 9 of 12 quarters; the other 3 were within.",
  "text.e63a1ad2145d75047b09": "source ids",
  "text.5afea51b8170efdb4865": "source ids · 1 records",
  "text.46985a666209dedadc1a": "AWS commitments were 496 bn, with a 6.4-year weighted-average remaining term and usage/performance conditions.",
  "text.7bc7f666b8f59b8d3d38": "counterexamples or limits",
  "text.0d08f3ff6adf64da49cc": "counterexamples or limits · 2 records",
  "text.40955ef059da1472f3c9": "Above-range results can reflect deliberate conservatism, not uniquely superior demand estimates.",
  "text.38f3af8983dcc09f7ddc": "Investment-linked customer financing complicates interpretation of backlog.",
  "text.fb46edfeb2921dafd9d8": "leadership attribution",
  "text.6bcde47b6c0234468c5f": "Jassy and the finance team own consolidated guidance. Garman became AWS CEO inJune 2024; earlier observations cannot be credited to his CEO tenure.",
  "text.bb6da0b898440c303261": "valuation use",
  "text.84418295b3b46677ae4a": "Apply to specific scenario conditions; no numeric credibility multiplier.",
  "text.2415cc3de90fc5b52e97": "Commercial scaling of custom silicon and AI services is evidenced; future product timelines remain uncertain.",
  "text.dea0ff72f95e8e6a54b9": "Medium.",
  "text.3df4801655a39ee31838": "Management said Trainium 3 had started shipping and Trainium 4 broad availability was about 18 months away.",
  "text.e3185ebb120a98156499": "Issuer reported AI and chip annualized revenue run-rates each above 25 bn.",
  "text.13da9a3975b3dcd404bb": "The run-rates overlap and are not audited independent revenue segments.",
  "text.de44751332d453d3006b": "Satellite and future chip milestones still depend on engineering, approvals and financing.",
  "text.86be21a2713ce291d7a0": "AWS delivery spans Garman, engineering teams and earlier chip investment; Jassy/board allocation is separate.",
  "text.890f44e6c71b63b516bf": "Rapid build-out has monetized, but constraints persist.",
  "text.e4032a0fbfe1f7dd920b": "Medium-high.",
  "text.314b99f8ca30e25c0e36": "AWS revenue 42.232 bn grew 36.7%; H1 net cash capex was 96.3 bn.",
  "text.fa2c56ecf69a47d66d8b": "Management reported 3.9 GW added in 2025 and targeted doubling power capacity by end 2027.",
  "text.e37ef92fd95e328d7e74": "Memory inflation can raise spending without equivalent capacity.",
  "text.a31dc61352ca136e35f6": "Power, construction and long-term energy commitments create execution and duration risks.",
  "text.2b6e3c99f483f3a43504": "AWS infrastructure, procurement and finance teams share responsibility; no sole-CEO causal claim.",
  "text.3dade9631fdefc579130": "Strong operating leverage, with accounting and one-off benefits requiring normalization.",
  "text.98098a852545b9835cc0": "High for reported results; medium for durability.",
  "text.80f2ac67f201ee62c99f": "Q2 EBIT27.461 bn included approximately 640 m tariff refunds and 551 m energy-derivative gains; excluding both still exceeded the guide.",
  "text.47f6e726b80e6c515878": "FY2025 North America EBIT29.619 bn and International EBIT4.750 bn demonstrate retail profitability.",
  "text.a1d0e447dcb8beae7a63": "Server useful-life changes affect comparability.",
  "text.50b4b985a20e7693e3de": "Severance, litigation and regionalization benefits are not perpetual efficiency gains.",
  "text.1f28403a8e090eec5d40": "Jassy, Stores leadership, AWS and finance all contribute; retail improvements are not attributed to Garman.",
  "text.9d79c1461fc302fb29ad": "Established cloud profits coexist with an unproven new AI investment cycle.",
  "text.b6646e8072d3a46daf09": "Medium-low for new-cycle returns.",
  "text.f24d55cac6c894e3c5e9": "TTM OCF161.403 bn versus net cash capex 169.007 bn produced negative 7.604 bn FCF.",
  "text.8e80521ff522c215c7f3": "Large private AI investments, customer funding and higher debt expand both upside and financing risk.",
  "text.422bb6849a24a1d71861": "Unrealized marks are not realized investment returns.",
  "text.23dd9300e68c6967b7bd": "Past AWS success does not establish current AI server life, pricing or customer credit quality.",
  "text.6842f895a319d3dbf5ee": "Board, Jassy and finance own capital allocation; Garman commentary informs operating assumptions but does not independently verify ROIC.",
  "text.28247b8a447bc137307b": "Research proposal only; all scenario parameters are analyst inference, not company guidance or consensus.",
  "text.bbb6d39ce5ab630f77f8": "implementation status",
  "text.3c023ec7e439c92d6b23": "Do not automatically replace production defaults until annual capital/lease/claims bridge is supported and reviewed.",
