  "text.9120c881177f324f07ac": "Search and Cloud continue growing, but AI delivery costs, capital intensity and regulatory risk temper long-run margins.",
  "text.4b3447037a7a555f1acb": "22% normalizes operating taxes above recent effective rates; very large non-operating equity gains make consolidated pretax-income tax ratios unsuitable as a direct operating forecast.",
  "text.027585c3ddc0f9d2a8c6": "0.7x requires $1.43 of net investment per extra $1 of revenue. The current AI buildout warrants much more capital than the historic search-only model.",
  "text.dca613b4a33aac4dbb73": "15% retains valuable distribution and software assets but reduces returns as competition and infrastructure intensity rise.",
  "text.0e543f2b6dffaff2856e": "0 means no additional user-entered claim beyond the separate explicit current claims model. Do not enter the same modeled claims again. The separate source-dated current claims model explicitly allocates mandatory preferred dilution/dividends, finance leases and noncontrolling claims, and adds a gross noncurrent-investment carrying proxy. Capped-call recovery, investment realization taxes and employee awards remain incomplete.",
  "text.4152f9766a72e271c5c1": "0 means no additional user-entered asset beyond the separate explicit current claims model. Alphabet already includes a gross noncurrent-investment proxy in that bridge; never add it again. No zero is proof of absence.",
  "text.4312128787b58c5d35e6": "Q2 2026 revenue was $119.8bn, up 24%, with a 34% operating margin; Google Cloud revenue rose 82%.",
  "text.a3cb679309ee6b84412e": "The separate source-dated current claims model explicitly allocates mandatory preferred dilution/dividends, finance leases and noncontrolling claims, and adds a gross noncurrent-investment carrying proxy. Capped-call recovery, investment realization taxes and employee awards remain incomplete.",
  "text.fab160a936d9aebd2e09": "Non-operating equity gains are excluded from operating income; no separate option value is assigned to Other Bets.",
  "text.a499f25bf640006105d6": "AI query economics, traffic acquisition and regulatory remedies",
  "text.8c443a25e5fda3a3dcab": "Mandatory-convertible preferred securities and non-marketable investment valuations",
  "text.b5089fa73783798e061f": "Cloud, advertising and other businesses have different economics. The book-capital proxy does not capitalize expensed R&D or fully strip investments.",
  "text.db9425d2f95ee5f97540": "Oclaro, NeoPhotonics and Cloud Light acquisitions changed the business mix, purchased intangibles and capital structure. Ten reported years are not a like-for-like decade of the current business. Optical-market cycles and returns from losses also affect comparisons.",
  "text.07a7f6d67552284beca0": "An optical connectivity ramp with lasting scale benefits, while current hypergrowth and peak product margins gradually normalize.",
  "text.2d2d0b595f41ed6585b7": "1.2x requires about $0.83 of net reinvestment per added $1 of sales. Capacity additions and working capital make the ramp less capital-light than a pure design/software business.",
  "text.4b9f37611ddf707fcca9": "14% retains a limited technology advantage while allowing competition and product replacement to erode peak returns.",
  "text.d74aa084afee3ece4610": "Fiscal Q4 2026 revenue was $1.006bn, up 109%; GAAP operating margin was 27.8%, compared with a 36.6% non-GAAP margin.",
  "text.cc09e5ba7443e7133433": "Review convertible-note conversion, capped-call treatment and employee dilution without counting the same instrument as both full debt and converted equity.",
  "text.efc984947b45c9eeba1c": "About 78% of modeled operating value comes after year 10. The result is highly dependent on mature margins, required reinvestment and discount rates.",
  "text.cd387e199ca9a2a97173": "The annual baseline lags the latest quarter’s ramp; a smooth ten-year path can understate early acceleration and overstate later growth.",
  "text.3d6806a9700ccb8d2b78": "800G/1.6T adoption, customer concentration and production yields",
  "text.086db52ac70b7e2981d0": "Price erosion, acquisitions and conversion/dilution of debt securities",
  "text.becd462e366522633b32": "source Ids · 4 records",
  "text.b4e5332424a35e397751": "Cash capital-spend guidance is not identical to economic additions; separately reconcile supplier payable changes, lease capitalization and asset commissioning.",
  "text.5ffc5889370ad37ae881": "Depreciation ramps with in-service timing, useful lives and hardware replacement, not merely spending date.",
  "text.bd2eefdf3125515fe9ff": "Cash taxes versus normalized operating taxes, interest and nonoperating income require a cash waterfall.",
  "text.4075c38ca3138b7ada13": "SBC must either remain an economic expense with consistent future share treatment, or be modeled through awards/dilution consistently; no double count.",
  "text.540fe5e5113f77b26d4a": "A lower cash deficit does not prove attractive incremental returns.",
