  "text.0ac8a04ce33cdcbe82d2": "FY2019 GAAP tax rate affected by $2.6bn tax benefit from intangible-property transfers; do not extrapolate as marginal rate.",
  "text.77f42ad4975fee3f9e94": "SBC is already an operating expense in GAAP EBIT; do not add back without dilution charge.",
  "text.87cfac29cb4f6e68286f": "Debt excludes leases by default; alternative totals provided. Do not add operating lease debt without corresponding operating-profit/cash-flow adjustment.",
  "text.c77ab835ad2e09398ff9": "Review employee option/RSU claims in original stock-based compensation note before claiming fully diluted common value.",
  "text.59e7c5caa15cce07e921": "Capex cash purchases omit finance-lease right-of-use additions; separate lease additions matter for reinvestment analysis.",
  "text.ba6439ee859356ed9657": "historical-case",
  "text.c21e990f24aa3d30b0e7": "FY2019 ended June 30, 2019",
  "text.4c61c71d29afa26cd383": "supplemental Evidence",
  "text.3c7de56b8418e5c27509": "supplemental Evidence · 4 fields",
  "text.169122657ec932584d27": "Original consolidated cash-flow statement; includes other adjustments, not pure D&A.",
  "text.6b15c751601f1f57402f": "Original stock-based compensation note stock-based compensation; 147m nonvested shares, grant-date weighted average fair value $78.49.",
  "text.d05ab75b002487bcc99f": "Original stock-based compensation note: $8.6bn unrecognized compensation over weighted average3yrs.",
  "text.a6da242e050abfbd63c2": "Original debt note, rounded $78.9bn fair value; not carrying value.",
  "text.5d224803045c5bfff28f": "Cloud and enterprise software sustain growth, while AI infrastructure reduces the capital efficiency of the historical software model.",
  "text.5fa8e2bf94a802f5c605": "18% begins near FY2026 reported growth. Azure and recurring enterprise subscriptions support the starting rate, which then fades to 2.5% as the revenue base expands.",
  "text.a6fd3329f0457eb1776f": "42% is below FY2026 operating margin of 46.8%. Recurring software remains profitable, but AI depreciation, inference costs and competition constrain permanent peak-margin extrapolation.",
  "text.0fcea5d58cadea7bd64d": "22% allows a higher normalized burden than FY2026 accounting tax of 19.4%; it does not extend discrete investment-related tax effects indefinitely.",
  "text.a60a5b7324c4a967694d": "0.6x means $1.67 of incremental net capital per extra $1 of revenue. FY2026 cash capex was $115.9bn; AI capacity makes an old asset-light software ratio inappropriate. It remains a normalized net-reinvestment assumption, not gross capex guidance.",
  "text.8e26c7fd1f8366fc8308": "16% assumes a persistent distribution and switching-cost advantage while fading returns as cloud infrastructure becomes a larger part of the business.",
  "text.de63c75dcf94fd76b79a": "9.5% nominal USD is a rounded model estimate. Assumed beta 1.0, 5% target debt and a 0.5-point debt spread reflect diversified recurring revenue and modest financing risk, with AI-demand uncertainty still present.",
  "text.c686662880af32f55714": "0 is an unreviewed placeholder, not evidence that no additional claims exist. Finance-lease obligations and non-operating investments are material. Lease capitalization must be reconciled with operating profit and reinvestment, not deducted a second time mechanically.",
  "text.2bb4db02b4cf3bb9d8ec": "MSFT-filing",
  "text.aa3b67643022170e552c": "FY2026 revenue was $331.8bn and operating income $155.2bn; Q4 revenue grew 18%.",
  "text.0d78d3fd3254ac03b2c3": "MSFT-release",
  "text.673368a25a1dda751c3e": "MSFT-annual-filing",
  "text.5ec117d2a79c02f50ef4": "Finance-lease obligations and non-operating investments are material. Lease capitalization must be reconciled with operating profit and reinvestment, not deducted a second time mechanically.",
  "text.19591623c851062263d1": "One sales/capital ratio smooths the front-loaded infrastructure buildout and may overstate early cash flow.",
  "text.e58fe82a7198938ec062": "AI monetization and customer returns on infrastructure spending",
  "text.92080b9cf099e9452798": "GPU useful lives, finance leases and capacity utilization",
